course: dictionary
lesson: 12479
title: Delegate: a person chosen, or to hand a task over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A delegate is a person chosen to speak, vote or act for a group. «Our class chose Priya as its delegate for the school council meeting.» Priya will speak for the whole class, so here delegate is a person.
explain: As a verb, to delegate means to give part of your work or a task to someone else to do. «Mr Hall delegated the tidying to three helpers.» The teacher handed the job over to other people, so here delegate is an action. Say it DEL-i-gate.
explain: Look for clues. Is there a person who speaks or votes for a group? That is the noun, said DEL-i-gut. Is someone passing a job to another person? That is the verb. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Delegate is a noun (DEL-i-gut) and a verb (DEL-i-gate).
fact: As a noun, a delegate is a person chosen to speak, vote or act for a group.
fact: As a verb, to delegate means to give part of your work, power or task to someone else.
fact: Delegates often meet at conferences, and the United Nations has delegates from many countries.
fact: Parents may delegate chores to children, and a good leader learns to delegate jobs in group work.
exercise: «Our school council has one delegate from each class.» What is a delegate here? | A type of school bag | A game played at break | A teacher who marks homework | *A person chosen to speak for a group
exercise: «Sam will delegate the cleaning to his team so he can finish the poster.» What does delegate mean? | To clean very carefully | To argue about a rule | *To give a job to someone else to do | To stop working altogether
exercise: «Ravi is the delegate for Year 5 at the conference.» Who is Ravi acting for? | His parents | *Year 5 | The teachers | The conference hall
test: «Mrs Lee delegated the planning to Ben and Chloe.» What did Mrs Lee do? | Planned the whole trip herself | *Gave the planning to Ben and Chloe to do | Cancelled the trip | Forgot all about the planning
test: «Each country sent a delegate to the United Nations meeting.» What is a delegate? | A large meeting room | *Someone sent to speak or vote for their country | A visitor who only watches | A type of country flag
exam: My teacher will delegate the register to me each morning. What does delegate mean here? | To cancel the register | To write a letter to the head | To count the children very quickly | *To hand a task over to someone else
